# v37 e2e suite: copy to `.env.e2e` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# Two TEST identities that log in through the real upstream (`UPSTREAM_AUTH_BASE_URL`), both in
# the dev `.env`'s ALLOWED_EMAILS. The admin one must be the dev ADMIN_EMAIL (v72: a dev-only
# override, since no test identity is the upstream's superuser), the other must not be. Never the owner's real account. Keep both dedicated to the suite: every run cancels
# anything they have in flight and archives the rest of their jobs. Register fresh ones freely
# (docs/LOCAL_DEV.md §4: two-step registration since upstream v2.2; reuse a slot's saved ones).
E2E_ADMIN_EMAIL=
E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
E2E_USER_EMAIL=
E2E_USER_PASSWORD=

# v71, optional: spec 28's dedicated MFA identity (TOTP on, allowlisted), never a shared one.
# Without it the spec is skipped. It runs in the desktop project only (single-use 30 s codes).
# E2E_MFA_EMAIL=
# E2E_MFA_PASSWORD=
# E2E_MFA_TOTP_SECRET=
# Opt-in, each spends what the account has little of: one wrong code (20 a day) / one unused
# recovery code (10 in all; remove it from your saved list afterwards).
# E2E_MFA_WRONG_CODE=1
# E2E_MFA_RECOVERY_CODE=

# Optional. The web origin of the local stack (default http://127.0.0.1:${WEB_PORT:-5173}, the dev `web`;
# v52: 127.0.0.1, not localhost, which can resolve to another server on [::1]).
# E2E_BASE_URL=

# `@network` spec only (`npm run test:e2e:network`): a Spotify track URL that is NOT yet in the
# dev ledger. The spec refuses one that is, since it would dedup instead of downloading, and a
# passing run puts it there, so pick a fresh one each time.
# E2E_NETWORK_TRACK_URL=
